1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,240
RenoGraph connects renovation tasks, materials and rooms in a live dependency graph.

2
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:09,483
Select a blocked task to see what is stopping it.

3
00:00:09,483 --> 00:00:13,725
Wavebinder single nodes hold facts; custom functions combine prerequisites and

4
00:00:13,725 --> 00:00:17,967
manual clearance, while complex nodes expose the resulting task state.

5
00:00:18,617 --> 00:00:21,827
Switching bathroom tiles to express delivery changes the

6
00:00:21,827 --> 00:00:24,637
forecast from October second to September thirtieth.

7
00:00:24,637 --> 00:00:27,045
Wavebinder multi nodes hold the choices.

8
00:00:27,045 --> 00:00:30,256
The selected option feeds availability, lead time and

9
00:00:30,256 --> 00:00:33,467
cost into dependent state and the project forecast.

10
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:37,383
Update quote runs a native Wavebinder HTTP GET.

11
00:00:37,383 --> 00:00:41,875
This demo supplier returns three-day delivery at twelve hundred fifty euros.

12
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:43,508
Watch the option update.

13
00:00:43,508 --> 00:00:46,775
An outage preserves the project, and retry recovers.

14
00:00:46,775 --> 00:00:51,267
Revision checks also prevent an outdated response from overwriting newer edits.

15
00:00:51,917 --> 00:00:55,935
Receiving the linked tile order marks the material delivered.

16
00:00:55,935 --> 00:01:01,738
Wavebinder propagates that fact into readiness, the forecast, and the room's material list.

17
00:01:01,738 --> 00:01:06,649
Each list contains complex material records, keeping delivery and price consistent.

18
00:01:06,649 --> 00:01:10,667
Professionals, purchases and supporting documents share the same workspace.

19
00:01:11,317 --> 00:01:16,719
Start bathroom plumbing, then complete it with six actual days instead of four.

20
00:01:16,719 --> 00:01:20,044
Its state propagates the variance into the forecast.

21
00:01:20,044 --> 00:01:22,122
Completed critical work becomes history.

22
00:01:22,122 --> 00:01:26,278
The dashed plumber connection explains why kitchen work must wait:

23
00:01:26,278 --> 00:01:30,433
RenoGraph calculates resource scheduling, and Wavebinder propagates the changed inputs.

24
00:01:31,083 --> 00:01:36,560
A scenario adds fourteen days and three hundred fifty euros to kitchen plumbing.

25
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:41,195
Completion moves from October second to October sixteenth, affecting six tasks.

26
00:01:41,195 --> 00:01:44,566
Changes propagate through an independently initialized Wavebinder runtime.

27
00:01:44,566 --> 00:01:49,200
The labelled snapshot lets us compare results without changing the baseline.

28
00:01:49,850 --> 00:01:54,000
Add bathroom snagging, then make it depend on fixture installation.

29
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,149
The new task becomes blocked, with its root cause visible.

30
00:01:58,149 --> 00:02:01,054
Structural changes build a replacement Wavebinder runtime;

31
00:02:01,054 --> 00:02:03,959
ordinary fact edits reuse the existing one.

32
00:02:03,959 --> 00:02:06,033
Each project keeps independent state.

33
00:02:06,683 --> 00:02:10,975
In a second tab, change snagging from one day to two.

34
00:02:10,975 --> 00:02:15,267
Return to the original tab: it has updated without a refresh.

35
00:02:15,267 --> 00:02:18,779
RenoGraph broadcasts committed revisions through server-sent events, then reloads

36
00:02:18,779 --> 00:02:21,900
one consistent workspace snapshot of the propagated state.

37
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:26,160
A manual inspection hold changes the task state.

38
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:31,124
Diagnostics show the mutation source and before-and-after values, making propagation inspectable.

39
00:02:31,124 --> 00:02:34,734
Wavebinder supplies reactive state; RenoGraph supplies renovation rules.

40
00:02:34,734 --> 00:02:40,600
Together, they turn a project plan into an explanation of what happens next.
